 Related biomedical work already connects uncertainty to annotation inspection and image quality control. AI$^2$Seg combines prediction confidence with annotation mismatch for instance-annotation inspection~\cite{schilling2023}; this setting has access to the annotations being inspected. Artifact augmentation addresses whole-slide-image quality control~\cite{jurgas2023}, whereas an instance-segmentation dataset study illustrates the importance of reporting detection and segmentation outcomes separately~\cite{reich2023}. These applications motivate explicit quality targets, but do not establish a ground-truth-free structural-failure detector for fracture CT. Reference-based quality estimation can introduce additional information beyond agreement~\cite{valindria2017}. Metric-selection frameworks likewise warn that the evaluation unit, matching rule, and target structure affect the meaning of reported performance~\cite{reinke2024,maier2024}.
 
-This study makes three contributions: it separates and tests the mechanisms of foreground and partition disagreement; compares both components and their combination against strong controls on a case-disjoint evaluation set; and examines how matching conventions, omission, and review cost change the conclusions. It reports successful contrasts together with stronger baselines and unsuccessful fusion attempts. The aim is to characterize when disagreement is informative, without assuming that its combined form must be superior.
+This study addresses three questions. What changes when foreground disagreement is separated from disagreement about fragment grouping? Does changing the partition normalization improve failure detection against strong component controls? Do those conclusions persist when failure definitions and review budgets change? We answer these questions using controlled perturbations, a separate evaluation cohort, and supplementary endpoint analyses. The contribution is an evidence-based account of what the scores measure and where they fail, rather than a claim that combining components must improve every quality-control task.
 
 \section{Methods}
 \subsection{Data, Models, and Evaluation Units}
 We used the public labeled PENGWIN 2026 Task~1 CT dataset~\cite{pengwin2026}. The evaluation involved 40 development scans and 100 additional scans, each balanced between pelvic and femur scan types. The latter were selected with a fixed seed from 210 eligible cases after excluding the initial training cases, development cases, and a separate local hold-back split. The local hold-back was not the official challenge test set and was not evaluated here. Case IDs, split hashes, and model manifests were checked. This establishes case separation; it does not independently establish patient-level separation across the source collection.
 
